  <region left="18" top="2417" width="500" height="88" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    <p bold="true">PART II: EVAPORATIVE CONCENTRATION MODEL &amp; DYNAMIC TEMPLATES</p>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2517" width="500" height="280" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Evaporative Physics in Cooling Towers:</p>
    <p bold="false">When makeup water is cycled in a cooling tower to N Cycles of Concentration (CoC), a fraction (1 - 1/CoC) of pure solvent water evaporates into the air stream, leaving all dissolved non-volatile mineral ions behind in the remaining 1/CoC mass of water.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">PHREEQC Reaction Formulation:</p>
    <p bold="false">For 1.0 kg of initial makeup water (55.508 moles H2O), the moles of water evaporated are:</p>
    <p bold="false">  n_evap = (1.0 - 1.0 / CoC) * 55.508  [moles H2O]</p>
    <p bold="false">This is cleanly executed via a REACTION block: 'REACTION 1; H2O -1.0; n_evap moles;'.</p>
    <p bold="false">The evaluation temperature is subsequently imposed using a 'REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1; T_val;' block.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">Dynamic String Array Construction (strrep + num2str Pattern):</p>
    <p bold="false">A base template containing symbolic tokens 'xevap' and 'xtemp' is dynamically populated inside procedural loops, avoiding any static XML boilerplate.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2809" width="132" height="117" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Cycles of Concentration (CoC) grid vector [-] (1 to 8 cycles)</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">coc_grid</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="operand">3</e>
    <e type="operand">4</e>
    <e type="operand">6</e>
    <e type="operand">8</e>
    <e type="operand">6</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="8">mat</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="2966" width="44" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Base cooling water script template with 'xevap' and 'xtemp' placeholder tokens</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">tmpl_cw</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">SOLUTION 1 Makeup Water; units mg/L; pH 7.8; temp 20; Ca 80; Mg 20; Na 50; Cl 60; S(6) 40; C(4) 120; REACTION 1; H2O -1.0; xevap moles; REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1; xtemp; SAVE solution 1; END</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
