  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="3030" width="500" height="88" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    <p bold="true">PART III: MULTI-TEMPERATURE PARAMETRIC SWEEPS ACROSS CoC</p>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="3130" width="500" height="184" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Three Characteristic Industrial Cooling Circuit Temperatures:</p>
    <p bold="false">  1. Basin / Cold Supply (T = 25°C): Cooling tower cold well supply to plant.</p>
    <p bold="false">  2. Warm Return / Summer Basin (T = 35°C): Return header from process units.</p>
    <p bold="false">  3. Heat Exchanger Tube Skin (T = 45°C): Hot process fluid contact boundary layer (highest scaling risk).</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">Procedural Loop Execution:</p>
    <p bold="false">For each CoC value, the loop computes n_evap, substitutes into tmpl_cw for all three temperatures, and evaluates Calcite SI, Gypsum SI, and solution pH via PhreeqcWrapper.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="3326" width="1608" height="515" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
