  <region left="18" top="4277" width="500" height="104" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    <p bold="true">PART IV: CALCITE SATURATION pH (pHs), LSI &amp; RSI AT HEAT EXCHANGER (40°C)</p>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="4393" width="500" height="408" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Langelier &amp; Ryznar Water Stability Theory:</p>
    <p bold="false">The Langelier Saturation Index (LSI) is defined as the difference between actual solution pH and the hypothetical saturation pH (pHs) at which the identical water would be at exact equilibrium with Calcite (SI = 0):</p>
    <p bold="false">  LSI = pH - pHs</p>
    <p bold="false">The Ryznar Stability Index (RSI) is an empirical indicator correlating scaling vs corrosive aggression:</p>
    <p bold="false">  RSI = 2·pHs - pH</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">Determination of pHs via PHREEQC Phase Equilibration:</p>
    <p bold="false">Rather than relying on simplified historical nomographs, PHREEQC computes exact pHs by equilibrating the concentrated solution with solid Calcite at target SI = 0:</p>
    <p bold="false">  'EQUILIBRIUM_PHASES 1; Calcite 0.0 10.0; SAVE solution 1; END'</p>
    <p bold="false">The resulting equilibrium pH read from this equilibrated solution copy is the exact, rigorous pHs.</p>
    <p bold="false"></p>
    <p bold="false">RSI Classification Scale for Cooling Water Systems:</p>
    <p bold="false">  • RSI &lt; 5.5: Heavy, dense CaCO3 scaling on heat exchanger tubes.</p>
    <p bold="false">  • 5.5 &lt;= RSI &lt;= 6.2: Moderate scaling tendency; manageable with antiscalant polymers.</p>
    <p bold="false">  • 6.2 &lt; RSI &lt; 6.8: Stable, neutral water; minimal scaling and minimal corrosion.</p>
    <p bold="false">  • 6.8 &lt;= RSI &lt;= 7.5: Significant corrosive tendency toward carbon steel equipment.</p>
    <p bold="false">  • RSI &gt; 7.5: Severe, aggressive acid/oxygen corrosion pitting.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="4813" width="44" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Template for concentrated cooling water at heat exchanger skin temperature (40 °C)</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">tmpl_hx</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">SOLUTION 1 Makeup Water; units mg/L; pH 7.8; temp 20; Ca 80; Mg 20; Na 50; Cl 60; S(6) 40; C(4) 120; REACTION 1; H2O -1.0; xevap moles; REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1; 40.0; SAVE solution 1; END</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="4893" width="44" height="24" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Template for calcite-equilibrated water determining exact Langelier pHs at 40 °C</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">tmpl_phs</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">SOLUTION 1 Makeup Water; units mg/L; pH 7.8; temp 20; Ca 80; Mg 20; Na 50; Cl 60; S(6) 40; C(4) 120; REACTION 1; H2O -1.0; xevap moles; REACTION_TEMPERATURE 1; 40.0; EQUILIBRIUM_PHASES 1; Calcite 0.0 10.0; SAVE solution 1; END</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    </input>
  </math>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="4957" width="1044" height="365" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <math>
    <description active="true" position="Top" lang="eng">
      <content>
        <p>Procedural loop computing actual pH, saturation pHs, LSI, and RSI at 40 °C heat exchanger surface</p>
      </content>
    </description>
    <input>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="operand">coc_grid</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">length</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">range</e>
    <e type="operand">coc_k</e>
    <e type="operand">coc_grid</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">eval</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">n_evap_k</e>
    <e type="operand">1.0</e>
    <e type="operand">1.0</e>
    <e type="operand">coc_k</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">/</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
    <e type="operand">55.508</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">eval</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">s_hx_k</e>
    <e type="operand">tmpl_hx</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">xevap</e>
    <e type="operand">n_evap_k</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">num2str</e>
    <e type="function" args="3">strrep</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">s_phs_k</e>
    <e type="operand">tmpl_phs</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">xevap</e>
    <e type="operand">n_evap_k</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">num2str</e>
    <e type="function" args="3">strrep</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">ph_act</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">s_hx_k</e>
    <e type="operand">db_phreeqc</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">phreeqc_pH</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">ph_sat</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">s_phs_k</e>
    <e type="operand">db_phreeqc</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">phreeqc_pH</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">si_c_hx</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand" style="string">Calcite</e>
    <e type="operand">s_hx_k</e>
    <e type="operand">db_phreeqc</e>
    <e type="function" args="3">phreeqc_si</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">lsi_val</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">ph_act</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">ph_sat</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">eval</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">rsi_val</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operand">2</e>
    <e type="operand">ph_sat</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">*</e>
    <e type="operand">ph_act</e>
    <e type="operand">k</e>
    <e type="function" args="2">el</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">-</e>
    <e type="function" args="1">eval</e>
    <e type="operator" args="2">:</e>
    <e type="operand">9</e>
    <e type="operand">1</e>
    <e type="function" args="11">line</e>
