  <region left="18" top="5462" width="500" height="88" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    <p bold="true">PART V: GRAPHICAL SATURATION &amp; STABILITY PROFILES (CHART2DLIB)</p>
    <p bold="true">=========================================================================</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="5562" width="500" height="120" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Figure 1: CaCO3 Calcite Scaling Potential — Calcite Saturation Index vs. Cycles of Concentration (CoC)</p>
    <p bold="false">Comparison between Cold Water Basin (25°C) and Hot Heat-Exchanger Tube Skin (45°C):</p>
    <p bold="false">Notice that Calcite SI is strictly positive (SI &gt; 0) at all cycles and increases sharply with CoC. The elevated temperature at 45°C further shifts SI upward due to retrograde calcite solubility.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="5694" width="540" height="280" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <xyplot width="540" height="280" points="6" smoothing="true">
    <propertiessource index="1" sourcetype="PropertyGrid" />
    <grid gridcolor="LightGray" gridpattern="Dash" gridthickness="1" isxgrid="true" isygrid="true" />
    <xaxes xmin="1.0" xmax="8.0" xtick="1.0" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <yaxes ymin="0.0" ymax="2.0" ytick="0.5" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <y2axes isy2axis="false" y2min="-1" y2max="1" y2tick="0.5" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <title2d title="CaCO3 Calcite Scaling Potential vs. Cycles of Concentration" titlefont="DejaVu Sans, 10pt" titlefontcolor="Black" />
    <xylabel labelfont="DejaVu Sans, 10pt" labelfontcolor="Black" tickfont="DejaVu Sans, 8pt" tickfontcolor="Black" xlabel="Cycles of Concentration (CoC) [-]" ylabel="Saturation Index SI = log10(IAP / Ksp) [-]" y2label="y2" />
    <legend isbordervisible="true" islegendvisible="true" legendbackcolor="200, 255, 255, 255" legendbordercolor="Black" legendfont="DejaVu Sans, 8pt" legendposition="SouthEast" textcolor="Black" />
    <traces>
      <trace seriesname="25 °C (Tower Basin Supply)" isy2data="false" isvisible="true" plotmethod="Lines" linecolor="RoyalBlue" linethickness="1" linepattern="Solid" symbolsize="8" symboltype="None" symbolborderthickness="1" symbolbordercolor="Black" symbolfillcolor="White" />      <trace seriesname="45 °C (Heat Exchanger Skin)" isy2data="false" isvisible="true" plotmethod="Lines" linecolor="Crimson" linethickness="1" linepattern="Solid" symbolsize="8" symboltype="None" symbolborderthickness="1" symbolbordercolor="Black" symbolfillcolor="White" />    </traces>
    <input>
      <e type="operand">curve_calcite_25</e>
      <e type="operand">curve_calcite_45</e>
      <e type="operand">2</e>
      <e type="operand">1</e>
      <e type="function" args="4" preserve="true">sys</e>
    </input>
  </xyplot>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="6069" width="500" height="104" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Figure 2: CaSO4 Gypsum Scaling Margin — Gypsum Saturation Index vs. Cycles of Concentration (CoC)</p>
    <p bold="false">Comparison between Basin (25°C) and Heat Exchanger (45°C):</p>
    <p bold="false">Gypsum remains strongly undersaturated (SI &lt; 0) across all operational cycles up to CoC = 8. Therefore, calcium sulfate scaling will not occur unless sulfuric acid (H2SO4) is severely overdosed.</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="6185" width="540" height="280" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <xyplot width="540" height="280" points="6" smoothing="true">
    <propertiessource index="1" sourcetype="PropertyGrid" />
    <grid gridcolor="LightGray" gridpattern="Dash" gridthickness="1" isxgrid="true" isygrid="true" />
    <xaxes xmin="1.0" xmax="8.0" xtick="1.0" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <yaxes ymin="-2.2" ymax="-0.6" ytick="0.2" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <y2axes isy2axis="false" y2min="-1" y2max="1" y2tick="0.5" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <title2d title="CaSO4 Gypsum Saturation Margin vs. Cycles of Concentration" titlefont="DejaVu Sans, 10pt" titlefontcolor="Black" />
    <xylabel labelfont="DejaVu Sans, 10pt" labelfontcolor="Black" tickfont="DejaVu Sans, 8pt" tickfontcolor="Black" xlabel="Cycles of Concentration (CoC) [-]" ylabel="Saturation Index SI [-]" y2label="y2" />
    <legend isbordervisible="true" islegendvisible="true" legendbackcolor="200, 255, 255, 255" legendbordercolor="Black" legendfont="DejaVu Sans, 8pt" legendposition="SouthEast" textcolor="Black" />
    <traces>
      <trace seriesname="25 °C (Tower Basin)" isy2data="false" isvisible="true" plotmethod="Lines" linecolor="DarkGreen" linethickness="1" linepattern="Solid" symbolsize="8" symboltype="None" symbolborderthickness="1" symbolbordercolor="Black" symbolfillcolor="White" />      <trace seriesname="45 °C (Heat Exchanger)" isy2data="false" isvisible="true" plotmethod="Lines" linecolor="DarkOrange" linethickness="1" linepattern="Solid" symbolsize="8" symboltype="None" symbolborderthickness="1" symbolbordercolor="Black" symbolfillcolor="White" />    </traces>
    <input>
      <e type="operand">curve_gypsum_25</e>
      <e type="operand">curve_gypsum_45</e>
      <e type="operand">2</e>
      <e type="operand">1</e>
      <e type="function" args="4" preserve="true">sys</e>
    </input>
  </xyplot>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="6560" width="500" height="104" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <text lang="eng" fontFamily="DejaVu Sans" fontSize="10">
    <content>
    <p bold="false">Figure 3: Plant Chemistry Stability Indices (LSI &amp; RSI) at Heat Exchanger Surface (40°C)</p>
    <p bold="false">Evaluation of Scaling Severity vs. Pipeline Corrosion:</p>
    <p bold="false">As CoC increases from 1 to 8, LSI increases from +0.33 to +1.18 (increasing scale potential), while RSI drops from 7.0 (stable/neutral) down to 5.2 (heavy scaling regime at CoC &gt;= 4).</p>
    </content>
  </text>
  </region>
  <region left="18" top="6676" width="540" height="280" color="#000000" fontSize="10">
  <xyplot width="540" height="280" points="6" smoothing="true">
    <propertiessource index="1" sourcetype="PropertyGrid" />
    <grid gridcolor="LightGray" gridpattern="Dash" gridthickness="1" isxgrid="true" isygrid="true" />
    <xaxes xmin="1.0" xmax="8.0" xtick="1.0" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <yaxes ymin="0.0" ymax="8.0" ytick="1.0" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <y2axes isy2axis="false" y2min="-1" y2max="1" y2tick="0.5" decimalplaces="3" numberformat="General" />
    <title2d title="Water Stability Indices (LSI &amp; RSI) vs CoC at 40 °C Exchanger" titlefont="DejaVu Sans, 10pt" titlefontcolor="Black" />
    <xylabel labelfont="DejaVu Sans, 10pt" labelfontcolor="Black" tickfont="DejaVu Sans, 8pt" tickfontcolor="Black" xlabel="Cycles of Concentration (CoC) [-]" ylabel="Stability Index [-]" y2label="y2" />
    <legend isbordervisible="true" islegendvisible="true" legendbackcolor="200, 255, 255, 255" legendbordercolor="Black" legendfont="DejaVu Sans, 8pt" legendposition="SouthEast" textcolor="Black" />
    <traces>
      <trace seriesname="LSI (Langelier Saturation Index)" isy2data="false" isvisible="true" plotmethod="Lines" linecolor="MediumVioletRed" linethickness="1" linepattern="Solid" symbolsize="8" symboltype="None" symbolborderthickness="1" symbolbordercolor="Black" symbolfillcolor="White" />      <trace seriesname="RSI (Ryznar Stability Index)" isy2data="false" isvisible="true" plotmethod="Lines" linecolor="Teal" linethickness="1" linepattern="Solid" symbolsize="8" symboltype="None" symbolborderthickness="1" symbolbordercolor="Black" symbolfillcolor="White" />    </traces>
    <input>
      <e type="operand">curve_lsi</e>
      <e type="operand">curve_rsi</e>
      <e type="operand">2</e>
      <e type="operand">1</e>
